{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1024655-the-most-practical-spheres","id":1024655,"title":"The most practical Spheres","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-31T00:48:49-08:00","id":1024655,"title":"The most practical Spheres","content":"I could have sworn a post like this had been made before, but I couldn't find one.<br /> <br /> I'll be running a game before long, and for the first time in awhile there will be people who have never played Mage. It bothers me that, in the interest of fairness and full disclosure, I'm going to feel compelled to tell them that certain Spheres at certain levels are just really practical to have. It would seem deceptive otherwise--like not pointing out Death of Obsidian Butterflies to new Twilight Caste players in 1E Exalted. But I'm afraid that they'll all want to glom onto those more practical powers, maybe to the detriment of more interesting and varied ones.<br /> <br /> What do I consider the most useful, at least in an obvious sense?<br /> <br /> As has been discussed here before, Prime 1 and Mind 1 are better than other level 1 abilities, because they go way beyond just sensing (though people vastly underestimate Time 1 and Correspondence 1). Prime 1 is essential if you want to use a lot of Quintessence, and Mind 1 can dramatically enhance a variety of mental tasks.<br /> <br /> Life 2 is the one that I have the hardest time arguing against everyone having. Self-healing, Bene Gesserit body control--but more important, it's required in a lot of conjunctional magic. I'm not talking about Sphere-bloated rotes from random supplements. I mean stuff mentioned in core books (or fairly straightforward extrapolations). Making a dynamically moving person invisible can be done with Forces alone (probably), but needs Life 2 to be at all efficient. Correspondence requires Conjunctional Life 2 to transport living things other than yourself until level 4. All kinds of other Correspondence stuff--Bans, linkages, etc. Using Time to affect an aspect of a living being but not the entire being (for instance reverting someone to physical youth but retaining their current memories).<br /> <br /> Matter 2. Everything I mentioned about Life 2 and conjunction applies to Matter 2 if you're talking about inanimate objects. Not as useful as Life 2 overall though.<br /> <br /> Prime 2, if you use Forces. Seriously, who uses a lot of Forces without Prime 2?<br /> <br /> Prime 3 if you have a Node--otherwise you can't use the Tass.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Nodes, Correspondence 2, if the game has any travel in it. Why take Node if you can't access it all the time?<br /> <br /> Am I missing anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T02:20:26-08:00","id":1024680,"title":"","content":"Entropy doesn't get flashy until 4 dots, but there are buttloads of practical things that can be done with Entropy 1-3, almost all of them coincidental.<br /> <br /> Depending on the elements of the setting you choose to emphasize, Spirit 2 could be absolutely essential or unnecessary esoterica practiced by a few shamans and mediums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T02:27:47-08:00","id":1024682,"title":"","content":"It depends a little on the broad picture:<br /> Setting<br /> Other spheres<br /> Spheres of the cabal<br /> Effects of Backgrounds(Wonder, Familiar, etc.)<br /> <br /> Personally I would go the extra dot and say Mind 2 to nudge many social situations to your favour.<br /> (Some others too)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T03:50:40-08:00","id":1024699,"title":"","content":"Important: Speaking paradigm-independently, and more importantly from a purely roleplay, everyday Mage life, awesome-to-have and not necessarily combatty-game-mechanics related aspect.<br /> <br /> I see <b>Life</b> as the most useful and versatile sphere to have. The ability to fix not only your health levels, but also all sorts of little blemishes, ailments and kinks, having control over the metabolism, the ability to temporarily raise physical attributes, the ability to sense life..it's great. And the cherry on top is Prime to conjure new life, of course.<br /> Oh, and of course the ability to have amazing hair days of any kind you prefer. Actually the I-want-to-have-this everyday usability applies to all classic pattern spheres, really:<br /> <br /> Second place would be <b>Forces</b> - the ability to create light, to drive away cold, to be able to heat things up or freeze them, night vision, the ability to move and lift things better with the aid of forces, having electricity just like that, etc...<br /> <br /> <b>Matter</b> would actually come in third place, as there simply is not often a reason to change the properties of matter in everyday mage life, unless you are a crafter. This sphere basically begs for Prime to be its lovely seasoning, as the cojuration of matter is, of course, absolutely great.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the non-classic pattern spheres, well. <b>Mind</b> is amazing, simply because of the multitasking and boosting abilities more than weird mind-reading or shielding. a wonderful combination of abilities to have for all sorts of tasks, especially when you are in a creative position and need to brainstorm - with yourself!<br /> <br /> Next, I can't decide between <b>Correspondence</b> or <b>Time</b> being the more handy sphere.<br /> Time of course lets you do things faster - and glimpse into the uncertain future or already-happened past. But I think I will have to go with Correspondence first, Time second, simply because of Correspondence's ability to scale things, to allow you to glimpse at far-away things, and of course teleportation.<br /> Yes, Correspondence first, then Time.<br /> <br /> <b>Entropy</b> and <b>Spirit</b> both are things that make the bottom of the list for me. Simply because Spirit really requires quite the way-of-life dedication in order to reap its benefits properly (Even for simple Umbra walking, because you better study up on all that could meet you there...). And Entropy, while being nice, is...not precise for everyday things, all in all. It's a nice addition to have to make your life easier, but unless you really have the sphere at higher levels, you don't quite have the control you need to make it a task oriented everyday thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prime</b>, of course, does not stand much on its own unless you specialize in Quintessence handling, which isn't all that useful for everyday stuff, but it is the oh so good bonus sphere to add to many of the above pattern spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-31-2016, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T04:20:58-08:00","id":1024705,"title":"","content":"Entropy 2 is one of the most versatile &quot;get stuff done&quot; spheres in the group. One of my players uses Entropy for almost everything. Finding people, not being seen, succeeding at physical tasks like throwing a rock at something...<br /> <br /> Correspondence is required to do anything at range. I can't tell you how man times my players have wanted to do flashy bits of magic only to be stopped by not being in the same room as the target. Things like telepathy with their mentor, looking for a Node with Prime, aiming attacks at hidden targets...<br /> <br /> Spirit can be he single most powerful sphere in the game or the most worthless waste of dots all dependant on what spirits you put in the game. If you have a player who is interested in the Spirit sphere, I'd say you have a duty to provide spirits for them and to prepare a bit of the spirit world in case they want step sideways.<br /> <br /> Matter is incredibly good, especially with Prime 2. Making stuff out of nothing never gets old. You might think Matter isn't as important as say Life, but if your mages ever find themselves locked up, or in front of a fence or barrier, Matter becomes the go to sphere for getting past this stuff. Want to disguse a mcguffin while taking it away? Matter. Want to make your clothes soak lethal? Matter. Want to turn Lead into Gold? Matter.<br /> <br /> My current players have been making great use of Mind aswell. One uses it all the time as a poor mans invisibility cloak, making themselves easier to ignore. Another uses it frequently to make a Mind Palace for covert communication in comfort.<br /> <br /> Forces is the best offensive sphere, so if you have a players who wants to be all fireballs and lightning, this is the sphere for them.<br /> <br /> Time 2 is ridiculous, especially when mixed with Entropy or Correspondence. Seriously, if you haven't planned your story around the possibility that your mage may be able to see through time, then Time 2 may easily destroy all tension and mystery. However, if Time starts to be abused, having the mage deal with more experienced Time mages could be just the ticket.<br /> <br /> In short, every sphere is useful depending on the need. Mixing spheres can make previously bland spheres incredible. Time 1 is the ultimate example of this, providing down-to-the-second precision with all your effects. Matter and Life for bizarre transformations. Mind and Spirit to read the minds of spirits. Entropy and Matter to make the world crumble or reinforce it. Prime, Time, and Forces to have security measures in the form of Fire.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend against telling them that certain spheres a &quot;better&quot; then others. You'll be starting them with your own biases on the spheres at best, and at worse encourage them to all start with the same spheres, limiting their ability to explore them.<br /> Instead, ask them what kind of mage they'd like to be and what kind of magic they want to do, then work with them to help them build that character.<br /> <br /> Have them feel the limitations of favouring certain spheres over others. Let them have &quot;sub-optimal&quot; builds. This will force them to me more creative with the spheres they do have.<br /> <br /> Besides, no matter which spheres they decide on, there will always be a point where they'll find te spheres they need for a particular effect are the ones they don't have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-03-2017, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T05:24:14-08:00","id":1024721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1024655-the-most-practical-spheres?p=1024705#post1024705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'d recommend against telling them that certain spheres a &quot;better&quot; then others. You'll be starting them with your own biases on the spheres at best, and at worse encourage them to all start with the same spheres, limiting their ability to explore them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to add, this needs underlining. as an ST, encourage your players to experiment and play. And if a player seems to consider a sphere bad purely because of the writing, give them examples of the things you can pull off with it.<br /> <br /> If everything fails, toss them against an enemy who pulls of awesome feats with a sphere they consider not good. It can be a verrrrry effective eye opener. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T05:53:33-08:00","id":1024732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1024655-the-most-practical-spheres?p=1024721#post1024721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to add, this needs underlining. as an ST, encourage your players to experiment and play. And if a player seems to consider a sphere bad purely because of the writing, give them examples of the things you can pull off with it.<br /> <br /> If everything fails, toss them against an enemy who pulls of awesome feats with a sphere they consider not good. It can be a verrrrry effective eye opener. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I totally highlight this points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T06:47:25-08:00","id":1024740,"title":"","content":"With new players I also explain by ease of use. We all know how great Spirit is but new players will often find it and Time to be more difficult and therefore less useful compared to other Spheres. Where as Life, Forces and Matter are relatively simple to understand. <br /> <br /> Gearing the beginnings of your Story to not require heavy use of the more complex spheres allows your players to get comfortable with the magick system with the more easily interpreted Spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T08:05:56-08:00","id":1024761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1024655-the-most-practical-spheres?p=1024740#post1024740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With new players I also explain by ease of use. We all know how great Spirit is but new players will often find it and Time to be more difficult and therefore less useful compared to other Spheres. Where as Life, Forces and Matter are relatively simple to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point.<br /> <br /> In my experience, the spheres most new players shy away from are:<br /> <br /> Corr: Because thinking in terms of non-euclidean space does not come naturally. (until they realise it's needed for any kind of range).<br /> Entropy: Since its write up can be a bit difficult to follow. A lot of new players look at it and think &quot;So... what does it actually do?&quot;<br /> Time: As it's a &quot;slow burn&quot; kind of sphere, with most of the classic time shenanigans reserved for higher levels.<br /> Prime: The worst offender. Most new players will need a lot of time and explanation to understand how this one works.<br /> <br /> Most new players I've whitnessed have no problems getting the basic &quot;physical&quot; spheres of Life, Matter, and Forces since that's the stuff they deal with in normal life. Same goes for Mind.<br /> Spirit is a bit of a wild card. Some players will ignore it entirely for the same reasons they might not get Entropy, others love the idea of being able to explore the Spirit World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T08:19:55-08:00","id":1024766,"title":"","content":"Entropy is one Sphere I try to encourage because I explain how it can effect the difficulty of almost any skill roll, ala luck. Most players usually understand that. It also helps that Entropy is one of the spheres that is widely useful at whatever rank you take it too. Unlike some spheres that though good have ranks that are weaker (Time) or not as useful after rank 3 unless its the backbone of your character's paradigm (Life can be seen this way many times)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T10:18:20-08:00","id":1024809,"title":"","content":"Prime is ok on it's own, but it's main utility comes with being paired with other spheres.<br /> <br /> Life is handy, but personally? I'd say correspondence is the most practical sphere for a new player. Honestly, a lot of things a new player could want can be obtained more safely by mundane means, and correspondence let's you obtain those means trivially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T12:56:46-08:00","id":1024874,"title":"","content":"Prime is problematic in that many of its uses are either too esoteric (pattern manipulation, sensing resonance), too Vulgar (pure energy blasts, rubbing the bones, unmaking people), or come a bit too late to be appealing for players with eyes towards the short term (Wonder creation, creating Nodes. I think a lot of new players wouldn't take Prime at all if not for the fact that it 1) is needed to create something from nothing, and 2) is required to have Quintessence points in excess of their Avatar rating.<br /> <br /> Which is a shame, because it has some functions that can be very useful. Prime 2 can make weapons deal Aggravated damage, and Prime 3 can do it with your bare hands. Likewise in both cases with soaking Aggravated damage, something vitally important if you get into combat and don't have Life or Matter at rank 3. You can't make Talismans or Periapts until later, but Prime 2/3 can be used to create Charm items (which, once you wrap your head around the mechanic, can be exceedingly appealing as a means of dodging magical Botches and distributing one's Effects to the rest of the Cabal). Even the simple ability to shapeshift, teleport, or step sideways, and have your pants come with you, can be a blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T13:03:03-08:00","id":1024877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1024655-the-most-practical-spheres?p=1024705#post1024705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd recommend against telling them that certain spheres a &quot;better&quot; then others. You'll be starting them with your own biases on the spheres at best, and at worse encourage them to all start with the same spheres, limiting their ability to explore them.<br /> Instead, ask them what kind of mage they'd like to be and what kind of magic they want to do, then work with them to help them build that character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. But when I tell them what the Spheres do, and what conjunctions are needed for a lot of Effects, there's a good chance they'll just follow the path of least resistance and the most useful combinations. Always going for more optimized characters can be limiting. Few people bother with Charisma in a D&amp;D Fighter for example, even though every memorable action hero is charismatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T19:45:20-08:00","id":1024983,"title":"","content":"Well, that is why I always played Bards, as my character was always the one who ended up being the party leader (or seen as the party leader by the NPCs because no one takes a Charisma 6 Dwarf fighter seriously). I think that it depends on how severely the ST enforces paradox. I always treated Correspondence effects as vulgar unless the PC could potentially have the object on their person (and could afford it with their Resources), so I never had to worry about players stealing massive numbers of grenades or gold bullion (it also forced players to live within their means). I always found Life, Mind, and Prime to be the most useful in my games myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T20:40:32-08:00","id":1024990,"title":"","content":"Rule wise, it's very difficult to create a system that encourages every option. D&amp;D Fighters aren't cut to be charismatic (albeit I can think worse combos than a warrior with CHA), and proving that &quot;game theory&quot; it's a thing, players thend to go there.<br /> <br /> This happens with a lot of stuff. In any WoD game players tend to take at least one combat Skill. This it's becuase combat it's someting that players just expect to happen sooner or latter.<br /> <br /> There are spheres that you will want to have, eventually (after learning the rules). Not because they're &quot;better&quot;, but because it's difficult to go arround without at least few dots in them.<br /> <br /> I think that the way to go (and I know it's not easy), it's to detach importance to these &quot;feats&quot;. If combat can be avoided, if friendly pnj can solve it, players will invest less in combat and more on social. If the story it's heavily political, and the combat can use a bit of social skill, maybe a warrior will think on buying a few dots in Charisma.<br /> <br /> In my experience, this can be solved (to a limmited extent) by reducing the importance of personal power. If taking &quot;less efficient&quot; choices doesn't lead to suicide/incompetence, it may be more tempting to choose flavorfull options. Easier said than done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T23:54:29-08:00","id":1025016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1024655-the-most-practical-spheres?p=1024983#post1024983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that is why I always played Bards, as my character was always the one who ended up being the party leader (or seen as the party leader by the NPCs because no one takes a Charisma 6 Dwarf fighter seriously). I think that it depends on how severely the ST enforces paradox. I always treated Correspondence effects as vulgar unless the PC could potentially have the object on their person (and could afford it with their Resources), so I never had to worry about players stealing massive numbers of grenades or gold bullion (it also forced players to live within their means). I always found Life, Mind, and Prime to be the most useful in my games myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that's why you use Correspondence to steal the things BEFORE you need them.<br /> <br /> I'm personally of the opinion that if you're actually casting effects during combat, you're either very confident or doing terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T00:41:40-08:00","id":1025024,"title":"","content":"Even so, I still considered it vulgar for characters to steal anything more valuable than their Resources because they were obviously trying to break the game (same thing with Life and Matter for high value items). Of course, you have to admire ingenuity. I had a player once who used Time effects to age brandy and whiskey. He would sell the centuries old stuff for a premium and, since he was not doing anything too broken, I allowed him to use coincidental effects, even though he was bending my rules a bit. Of course, I eventually required him to spend XP to increase his Resources before anything got too silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:40:06-08:00","id":1026035,"title":"","content":"Resources is your ability to, through regular channels, obtain material goods. It's your career and whatnot.<br /> <br /> If you feel like making a solid gold palace with matter, well you didn't obtain that through regular material goods. But someone who only does business in gold bars is certainly going to attract attention from the wrong kind of people.<br /> <br /> Basically, you're MOST at risk for being outted when you try to stand half-in half-out of the system. If you go off the grid, live in a little place in the middle of nowhere, ward it to hell and back so nobody can find you, and supply all your needs with sphere magic. Either yours or your chantry-mates. Then you're safe.<br /> <br /> If you live in a city, go to work, and supply all your needs with Resources 4-5. Then you're also pretty safe. Especially if you don't use magic at all.<br /> <br /> It's when you start using sphere magic to make gold bars and try to peddle them out the back of your truck for twinkies and beer that you run into problems.<br /> <br /> It's not game breaking, because it's not representative of what Resources is. Now if they want to argue they're doing this all the time and thus they should have a steady income from it? That's a solid reason for a buy up in the Resources merit. And also one hell of a plot hook to sic the Syndicate on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:40:33-08:00","id":1026080,"title":"","content":"Exactly.<br /> IMO the game is about choices and the resulting consequences.<br /> Let them conjure what the hell they want, and go from there.<br /> Resonance, Paradox and plain mundane consequences give you plenty of hooks to draw from.<br /> As it is said: \u201cFavour saying \u201cYes\u201c over saying \u201cNo\u201c because saying yes is more entertaining.\u201c","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:19:55-08:00","id":1026105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1024655-the-most-practical-spheres?p=1026080#post1026080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly.<br /> IMO the game is about choices and the resulting consequences.<br /> Let them conjure what the hell they want, and go from there.<br /> Resonance, Paradox and plain mundane consequences give you plenty of hooks to draw from.<br /> As it is said: \u201cFavour saying \u201cYes\u201c over saying \u201cNo\u201c because saying yes is more entertaining.\u201c</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't be said better. More so in Mage than any other RPG I don't so no you cant do that (through magick). You may not have the spheres needed or the ability to run the ritual long enough but its always possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}